\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  \cf0 'For my sake and the Gospel's, go
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj And tell redemption's story';
\par His heralds answer 'Be it so';
\par And Thine, Lord, all the glory!
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj They preach His birth, His life, His cross
\par The love of His atonement
\par For whom they count the world but loss,
\par His Easter, His enthronement.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Hark! Hark! The trump of jubilee
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Proclaims to every nation,
\par From pole to pole, by land and sea,
\par Glad tidings of salvation;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj As nearer draws the day of doom,
\par While still the battle rages,
\par The heavenly dayspring, through gloom,
\par Break on the night of ages.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Still on and on the anthems spread
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Of  hallelujah voices;
\par In concert with the holy dead,
\par the warrior Church rejoices;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj their snow-white robes are
\par washed in blood,
\par their golden harps are ringing;
\par earth and the Paradise of God
\par one triumph song are singing.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  He comes whose advent-trumpet drowns
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj The last of time's evangels,
\par Immanuel, crowned with many crowns,
\par The Lord of saints and angels.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj O life, light, Love, the great I AM
\par Triune, who changest never,
\par The throne of God and of the Lamb
\par \pard       Is Thine, and Thine forever.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

